Firmware: AMD Navi10 GPU firmware from linux-firmware 20260410: the
          security processor's secure OS, the display security
          application, the system-management unit, the graphics pipe
          (PFP, ME, CE), the compute processors (MEC, MEC2), the run-list
          controller (RLC) and the copy engines (SDMA0, SDMA1)
Hardware: AMD Radeon RX 5600 and RX 5700 (Navi10, RDNA1), used by the
          amdrdna driver (CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_AMDRDNA)
Files:    /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_sos.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_asd.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_smc.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_pfp.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_me.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_ce.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_mec.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_mec2.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_rlc.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_sdma.bin
          /lib/firmware/amdgpu/navi10_sdma1.bin
Source:   linux-firmware tag 20260410 (commit dc85ccedc9c973682fbcf4d628ca61174bcc3120)

